;; Maps conj2026 sessions to their pre-existing Google Calendar event ids on the
;; "Clojure Conj 2026" calendar. `bin/sync-gcal` only ever updates events listed
;; here -- it never creates or deletes events, so adding a new event to the
;; calendar (via the web UI) and then adding its id here is how you opt it into
;; automatic syncing.
;;
;; :gcal/title-override lets a specific event keep custom title styling
;; (e.g. the keynote asterisks) instead of the computed "{title} — {subtitle}".
;;
;; Deliberately excluded: the Closing Party event
;; (vs5sqgg7b6c7q7hacutq74va98) -- it was hand-edited after creation (custom
;; `location` field, a calendar label, a reminder override) and the Calendar
;; API's events.patch has no way to preserve a `location` field it isn't told
;; about, so an automatic sync would silently wipe it. Sync that one by hand.
